From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: geramyloveless <gloveless@jqluv.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:27:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Loom] Address K/V fragments through borrowed device
 addresses

buffer.from_address forms a non-owning global buffer root from a native
64-bit device address, with a byte length and base alignment the caller
guarantees. It does not allocate, retain or grant noalias storage. On
AMDGPU such a root may differ between lanes and is not an ABI buffer
binding, so its accesses always take the flat address form with the full
address in vector registers.

A range assertion (index.assume) on an address that proves it fits fewer
register units now keeps the low units of the wider producer instead of
aliasing it.

libhrx gains hrx_buffer_get_device_address, which borrows a buffer's native
device address without mapping it for host access.
